<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">February Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1917</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The February Revolution of 1917 was the uprising in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/petrograd">Petrograd</a> that forced the abdication of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nicholas-ii">Nicholas II</a>. It ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-romanov">Romanov</a> monarchy and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>, establishing a provisional government that was overthrown by the Bolsheviks later that year.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/february-revolution.jpg" alt="February Revolution" width="320" height="193" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jones, Stinton · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Manifestaci%C3%B3nAFavorDeLaRep%C3%BAblicaPetrogrado1917--russiainrevolut00jone.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
